//RS /// Classify a ref with workspace-member awareness (Slice B, D-MONOREF1=A).
//RS ///
//RS /// Resolution order, first match wins:
//RS ///   1. source forms `package@source` and `source.package` — via `classify_in`
//RS ///   2. local form  `./package` — via `classify_in`
//RS ///   3. path form   `infra/logging` — exact relative-path match in the index
//RS ///   4. bare form   `logging` — exact member-name match in the index
//RS ///
//RS /// The source form is tried first so an explicit source suffix always wins
//RS /// over an accidental index collision. Only a ref with no source suffix (what
//RS /// `classify_in` reports as `MissingSeparator`) falls through to the index. A
//RS /// path/bare ref that matches no member is `UnknownMember` (E1231); one that
//RS /// matches more than one is `AmbiguousMember` (E1230).
